# Shared secret the promote-receive function checks before writing anything.
# Same value in BOTH places: your local .env AND the production site's
# environment variables (Netlify dashboard > Project configuration >
# Environment variables). Generate one with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
PROMOTE_SECRET=

# Only set this locally (in your own .env, never in the production site's
# env vars). It's how your local admin-promote function knows where "prod"
# is. Prod has nowhere further to promote to, so it should NOT have this
# set — leaving it unset there is what makes the promote button correctly
# report "not configured" if someone clicks it on the live site.
PROD_SITE_URL=https://your-site-name.netlify.app
=======
# There are two separate pieces to this, don't confuse them:
#
# 1. PROMOTE_SECRET — set this on EVERY receiving site (each Netlify
#    project you promote brands into: your main production site, and any
#    additional per-branch sites). Each site gets ITS OWN distinct value,
#    generated with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. This is what
#    admin-promote-receive.ts checks before writing anything. Using the
#    same secret across multiple sites means a single leaked value can
#    write to all of them — don't do that.
PROMOTE_SECRET=

# 2. PROMOTE_TARGETS — set this ONLY in your local/dev .env (the
#    environment that SENDS promotes). It's a JSON array listing every
#    site you can promote to, and must include the matching secret you
#    set as that site's own PROMOTE_SECRET above. The /admin screen reads
#    this (via /api/admin/promote-targets, name + url only, secrets never
#    reach the browser) to populate the destination dropdown.
#
#    Example with two targets:
#    PROMOTE_TARGETS=[{"name":"Production","url":"https://assistivan-demo.netlify.app","secret":"<that site's PROMOTE_SECRET>"},{"name":"PharmaEssentia","url":"https://pharmaessentia-demo.netlify.app","secret":"<that site's PROMOTE_SECRET>"}]
#
#    Do NOT set PROMOTE_TARGETS on any deployed site — it has nowhere
#    further to promote to, and leaving it unset there is what makes the
#    Promote button correctly refuse to run if clicked on a live site.
PROMOTE_TARGETS=
